  "answer": "The study met only part of the goal: 2 of the 5 cases were confirmed, so it does not give a full top 5. The two cases are scene 02eadd92 at the recorded speed and timing (S2) and scene 054b5901 at 1.2\u00d7 speed and the recorded timing (S6). Every repeat at each failed, but with only a few repeats per setting the ranges show only that the failure rate is above about one half. Neither case shows that the crossing car's timing matters. In both scenes the policy ignored the RIGHT command and drifted left. On 02eadd92 it rear-ended the crossing bus. On 054b5901 it ran onto the median with no car nearby. Every failure is flagged as a possible artifact because the ego ended more than 3.5 m from the recorded path. The video and log review shows that this gap comes from the policy's own steering, not from rendering.",
